1. Project Overview

The QR-Based Digital Menu & Ordering System is a web-based platform designed to simplify the ordering process inside cafés and restaurants.

Instead of relying on physical menus and manually communicating orders to the cashier, customers can scan a single QR code available in the restaurant, select their table number, browse the digital menu, choose multiple products, and submit their order directly to the cashier system.

The system consists of three main actors:

Customer: Browses the menu, selects products, enters the table number, optionally provides their name, and submits an order.
Cashier: Monitors incoming orders, reviews their availability, and accepts or rejects orders.
Admin: Manages menu categories and products, including their prices and availability, and monitors sales and operational KPIs through a dashboard.

Orders are initially stored in a relational operational database. At the end of each week, the collected operational data is transferred to a Data Warehouse to support historical analysis and reporting.

The Admin can access a dashboard containing KPIs and analytical insights for a selected period, such as weekly or previous-period sales and order performance.

2. Project Objectives

The main objectives of the project are:

2.1 Improve Customer Ordering
Provide customers with a simple digital menu accessible through a QR code.
Allow customers to order multiple products without requiring an account or application installation.
2.2 Improve Order Management
Allow cashiers to receive incoming orders directly through the system.
Allow cashiers to accept or reject orders based on product availability and operational conditions.
2.3 Reduce Ordering Errors
Digitize the ordering process and reduce errors caused by manual order entry or verbal communication.
2.4 Centralize Menu Management
Allow the Admin to create, update, and delete product categories and menu items.
Allow the Admin to define product prices and availability.
2.5 Enable Data-Driven Analysis
Store operational order data in a relational database.
Transfer historical data to a Data Warehouse on a weekly basis.
Provide the Admin with KPIs and analytical dashboards based on historical and operational data.

3. Project Scope

3.1 Customer Scope

The system will allow customers to:

Access the digital menu by scanning the restaurant QR code.
Enter or select their table number.
Browse available product categories and products.
View product names, descriptions, and prices.
Select multiple products and specify quantities.
Review the order and total price.
Optionally provide their name.
Submit the order to the cashier.
3.2 Cashier Scope

The system will allow the Cashier to:

Access a secured order management interface.
View incoming orders with their table numbers, products, quantities, and prices.
Review the availability of requested products.
Accept valid orders.
Reject orders when one or more requested products are unavailable or the order cannot be fulfilled.
Update the order status after handling the order.

If a customer submits an order containing a product that is no longer available, the system will allow the Cashier to reject the pending order. The order will then be marked as REJECTED instead of being confirmed.

3.3 Admin Scope

The system will allow the Admin to:

Create, update, and delete product categories.
Create, update, and delete products.
Set product prices.
Manage product availability.
Monitor orders and sales-related KPIs.
View analytical dashboards for selected periods.
Access historical sales and operational reports generated from the Data Warehouse.
3.4 Data & Analytics Scope

The system will use two main data layers:

Operational Database

The relational operational database will store current system transactions and operational data, including:

Orders
Order Items
Products
Categories
Tables
Order statuses
Product prices
Customer names when provided
Data Warehouse

Historical operational data will be transferred to the Data Warehouse at the end of each week.

The Data Warehouse will support analytical queries and dashboards covering metrics such as:

Total Orders
Total Revenue
Average Order Value
Accepted Orders
Rejected Orders
Order Trends
Top-selling Products
Popular Categories

The Admin will be able to use these analytical insights to monitor the restaurant's sales and operational performance over a selected period.
